    "extraction_notes": [
      "SHA-256 of source PDF verified: 7ee99c2ff94d07a981fa018ea9c1b86302d179fbff5a466d29e21bebd6eba617.",
      "Method: pdftotext -layout for tables, then pdftoppm 200 dpi page renders with programmatic pixel tracing for curves (axis frames located by full-row/full-column dark-pixel runs, curves sampled per column with gridline-thickness filtering, sample columns offset to avoid vertical gridlines).",
      "Fig 6 calibration: x 260 px = 0 V, 111.25 px/V; y 837 px = 0 A, 393 px = 0.4 A. Fig 10 calibration: x 260 px = 0 V, 148.33 px/V; y 831 px = 0 A, 387 px = 0.6 A. Fig 13 calibration: x 948 px = 0.1 V, 148 px/decade; y 1180 px = 100 pF, 222 px/decade.",
      "Digitized capacitance curves cross-check against Table 7 anchors at VDS = 10 V: Ciss read ~4.14e-11 F vs typ 4.2e-11 F; Coss read ~7.1e-12 F vs typ 7e-12 F; Crss read ~3.5e-12 F vs typ 4e-12 F.",
      "Transfer curve cross-check: local slope near ID = 0.2 A at 25 degC is about 0.63-0.66 S, consistent with gfs typ 0.7 S (Table 7). VGS = 10 V output curve slope ~1 A/V is consistent with RDSon typ 1 ohm.",
      "One Fig 13 sample at VDS = 1.6 V (5.26e-11 F) was rejected as contamination from the '(1)' curve-label text; surrounding samples (0.65, 1.45, 2.8 V) form a smooth trend and were kept.",
      "VGS = 1.25 V output curve omitted: it hugs the ID = 0 axis (below ~0.007 A) and could not be digitized reliably at this resolution.",
      "All quantities are SI: capacitances in farads, currents in amperes, resistances in ohms. Datasheet pF/mA table values converted accordingly.",
      "No vendor SPICE or model-pack data used; public Nexperia product data sheet only."
    ],
